{
  "requirement": "`habeas_sdk::domain::NodeContents::format` presents the retained\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_contents` as text for an agent:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait NodeContents: Send + Sync {\n    /// Present these retained contents as text for an agent.\n    /// Use the same observation described by fingerprint().\n    /// Everything needed for presentation is retained in this value.\n    fn format(&self) -> String;\n\n    // ... fingerprint method introduced below ...\n}\n```\n\nFormatting uses the retained value and completes without further resource reads\nor fallible preparation.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately cover `requirements.sdk.graph.fingerprint_content.format`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the requirement**\n1. `format` presents the retained node contents as text for an agent.\n2. It uses the same observation that `fingerprint()` describes.\n3. Everything needed is retained in the value.\n4. Formatting does no further resource reads and no fallible preparation.\n\n**Coverage**\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` is marked `{test}` for this requirement.\n  - It reads a snapshot while the graph content is \"before\".\n  - It asserts `snapshot.content.format()` is \"before\".\n  - It then changes the graph content to \"after\".\n  - It asserts `format()` is still \"before\", and that `fingerprint()` equals the snapshot fingerprint (value \"before\").\n  - It asserts the graph's recorded `reads` are still exactly `[1]`.\n  - Together these cover obligations 1–4 at the trait level. Formatting uses retained data, makes no second read, and matches the fingerprinted observation.\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement]` is marked `{test}` for this requirement.\n  - It builds `HabeasNodeContent` from an already-resolved input that points at a non-existent file (`missing.rs`).\n  - It asserts `format()` succeeds and contains both the supplied text and the path.\n  - So formatting works from the retained value without touching the filesystem and without a fallible step.\n\n**Implementations**\n- `HabeasNodeContent`'s `format` returns `self.text.clone()`. The text is built once in `prepare`, together with the fingerprint, from the same resolved input and selector. `format` itself has no conditional or transformation, so it is covered by the tests above.\n- `ReviewContent`'s `format` in `src/authoring/sdk.rs` has the same shape: a retained string field with the fingerprint produced in `node_content`.\n- `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[review_graph_delegates_unprepared_sources_and_paths_to_the_domain]` also asserts on `format()` output. It is not marked for this requirement. Because the `format` body it exercises is a pass-through, I don't treat this as a material gap.\n\nI found no plausible violating behavior that these tests would accept.",
  "references": "a2a627f384814594a5df14493a6dd913d509079102eaab66421fdc0ebd744fbb",
